ref 17592186515232 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515495 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515281 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515495 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515495 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515495 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186514937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515495 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ce83d198-e8da-5698-936e-5f3c729fa5e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515516 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186514925 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515516 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186514947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515516 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186514973 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515516 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515516 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515516 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515516 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515516 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186515370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515516 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ff6b6508-4543-52e8-9082-8cfcb40a4f2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515522 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515522 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132395" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515522 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515522 #edb/ref 1071 "Which digits, when inserted into the blank, make the number $◻46\\,283\\,123$ divisible by $3?$\n\nI. $3$\n\nII. $6$\n\nIII. $9$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515522 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "09796f32-bb96-5a23-99aa-3f951bba421d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515522 #edb/ref 1074 "A number is divisible by $3$ if the sum of its digits is divisible by $3.$\n\nFor the number $◻46\\,283\\,123$ the sum of the digits is\n\n$$\n◻+4+6+2+8+3+1+2+3=29+◻.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each of the given digits that could be inserted into the blank.\n\n- If we insert $3$ into the blank, then the sum of the digits is $29+3=32,$ which is *not* divisible by $3.$\n\n- If we insert $6$ into the blank, then the sum of the digits is $29+6=35,$ which is *not* divisible by $3.$\n\n- If we insert $9$ into the blank, then the sum of the digits is $29+9=38,$ which is *not* divisible by $3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515531 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515531 #edb/ref 1069 "q-99747" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515531 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515531 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of $0÷132.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515531 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2e7b9d53-ca77-5eb9-b2d4-ae5998fd670b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515531 #edb/ref 1074 "Zero divided by any number (other than zero) equals zero. Therefore, $0÷132=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515549 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515455 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515549 #edb/ref 1069 "q-59573" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515549 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515549 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following shows the point $C(4,-2)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515549 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5fcefc3b-3a62-52cf-8d40-3f5f5111128b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515549 #edb/ref 1074 "Starting at the origin, we move along the $x$ and $y$ axes to get to the point $C.$\n\nFirst, we move along the $x$-axis. The point $C$ has an $x$-coordinate of $4,$ so we move $4$ units to the *right*, in the positive direction of the $x$-axis.\n\nThen, we move along the $y$-axis. The point $C$ has a $y$-coordinate of $-2,$ so we move $2$ units *down*, in the negative direction of the $y$-axis.\n\n![](images/68/68f55dd9851c7fa3805dec284aad2a9eb7e07b77a94a3f6b4b9b8ddcfd630baf.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515552 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515441 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515552 #edb/ref 1069 "q-59891" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515552 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515552 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/ae/aeee7aa14daab059cc6a03a3fd7437799713009014d21a5b8751f073864cf959.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of pentagons to the total number of shapes?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515552 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "65505664-38a4-5c26-b1d6-fe28649569b3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515552 #edb/ref 1074 "We count the number of pentagons. We see that there are $2$ pentagons.\n\nWe count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $4$ shapes in total.\n\nSo the ratio of pentagons to total shapes is $2:4.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers in a ratio by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,4 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,2 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of pentagons to the total shapes is $1:2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515567 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515567 #edb/ref 1069 "q-350261" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515567 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515567 #edb/ref 1071 "Maya and Priya are café owners. In the previous season, $55%$ of Maya’s orders were takeout, while the decimal proportion of Priya’s orders that were takeout was $0.8.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Less than half of Maya's orders were takeout.\n\nII. More than half of Priya's orders were takeout.\n\nIII. Maya had a greater percentage of takeout orders compared to Priya." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515567 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8134e1ae-9578-5877-ab86-0666cefb2b4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515567 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n55%>50%,\n$$\n\nmore than half of Maya's orders were takeout.\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n0.8>0.5.\n$$\n\nSo, more than half of Priya's orders were takeout.\n\n- Statement III is false. We can compare $55%$ and $0.8$ by converting the decimal into a percent. \n\nTo do this, we multiply it by $100:$\n\n$$\n0.8\\times 100=80%\n$$\n\nSince  $55%<80%,$ Maya did not have a greater percentage of takeout orders compared to Priya.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515568 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515516 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515568 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75558" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515568 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515568 #edb/ref 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"Nine more than a number.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515568 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "82e0c6bc-08da-5baa-b6ef-f85a33295d8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515568 #edb/ref 1074 "If we denote our number by $a$, then the phrase \"nine more than a number\" can be written as\n\n$$\na+9.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515579 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515579 #edb/ref 1069 "q-98372" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515579 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515579 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are natural numbers?\n\nI. $4$\n\nII. $-1$\n\nIII. $0$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515579 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9f63b51c-dc94-5351-8801-eb6438eefe9b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515579 #edb/ref 1074 "The natural numbers consist of all positive whole numbers.\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,5,…\n$$\n\nOf the given numbers, $4$ is a natural number, but $-1$ and $0$ are not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515582 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515475 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515582 #edb/ref 1069 "q-2089" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515582 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515582 #edb/ref 1071 "$3-7=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515582 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a1cd61ea-798a-5042-9adf-ebc8c5167849" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515582 #edb/ref 1074 "To subtract $7$ from $3$, we start at $3$ on the number line and move $7$ places to the left. \n\n![](images/c5/c520527df91b786ff936ed3061e7596b9504ccdc9d959236a7daeba5f795654c.png)\n\nThis gives $3-7=-4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515588 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515588 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60253" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515588 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515588 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/72/7237864f8c4c8711820ced0d2acad7a098e71a1965730e118eeed65f79bc496a.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of rhombuses to circles?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515588 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b2e2b3d0-06c7-5374-8f2a-5e2b0c04b187" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515588 #edb/ref 1074 "We count the number of rhombuses. We see that there are $3$ rhombuses.\n\n We count the number of circles. We see that there are $2$ circles.\n\nSo the ratio of rhombuses to circles is $\\frac{3}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515611 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515611 #edb/ref 1069 "q-43032" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515611 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515611 #edb/ref 1071 "$4\\cdot (-3.5)=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515611 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e4257f22-304f-5aae-a7d4-d381f535406f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515611 #edb/ref 1074 "We have a product of a positive number $(4)$ and a negative number $(-3.5).$ So the product will be negative:\n\n$$\n4\\cdot (-3.5)=-\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $4$ by $3.5$ without any signs: $4\\cdot 3.5=14.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n4\\cdot (-3.5)=-14.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1